(34)  For the purpose of this Procedure:
  1. graded assessment: any assessment for which marks contribute towards a student’s final grade for a subject;
  2. hurdle assessment: any assessment for which a pass is required in order for a student to pass a subject;
  3. Professional Equivalence: a status conferred on an individual who, while not meeting the formal qualifications specified for the AQF level at which they are teaching, is assessed to have qualifications and/or experience at a level deemed equivalent to the required level in the relevant cognate area;
  4. staff supervision: the process by which a staff member without Professional Equivalence is guided by a more senior member of staff to ensure that the supervised staff member engages in: 
    1. teaching duties that are appropriate for their level of qualification;
    2. professional development that progresses their ability to meet Professional Equivalence at a future date.

