(36)  For the purposes of assessing fees and load reporting an EFTSL (Equivalent Full-Time Student Load) for an academic year is defined as 120 credit points.
(37)  Enrolment load is calculated per half year:
  1. for completion monitoring, a student is considered full-time when their EFTSL is 0.5 (ie 60 credit points) or above per half year;
  2. for the purposes of meeting conditions for Australian government assistance , or for calculating student amenities fees, students are considered full-time when their Equivalent Full-Time Study Load (EFTSL) is 0.375 or above per half year. 


(38)  Below these values, a student is considered part-time. 
(39)  Courses at La Trobe have a maximum allowable credit-point enrolment depending on the requirements of the specific course and the structure of the teaching periods:
  1. the summer teaching period and semester-based courses have a typical maximum enrolment of between 60 credit points per semester or teaching period;
  2. term-based courses have a typical maximum enrolment of 30 credit points per term;
  3. courses that fall into non-standard teaching periods have a maximum enrolment of between 60 to 75 credit points per teaching period.


