(69)  The University may alter, suspend, or cancel a student’s enrolment where:
  1. a penalty of suspension or exclusion is to be applied as a result of a finding under the [General Misconduct Statute 2009](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/directory/summary.php?legislation=37) or the [Academic Integrity Statute 2015](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/directory/summary.php?legislation=36);
  2. the student has failed to make satisfactory academic progress as defined by the [Academic Progress Statute 2010](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/directory/summary.php?legislation=82);
