(23)  Professional Staff are eligible to request ad hoc, short term or regular Hybrid Working Arrangements in accordance with clause 53 of the [Enterprise Agreement](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/download.php?id=422&version=2&associated).
(24)  Depending on the circumstance for the request, Professional and Academic staff may be eligible to make a request for a Flexible Working Arrangement in accordance with the [Flexible Working Policy](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=88). Staff should review the eligibility criteria within the [Flexible Working Policy](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=88) before making a request for a Hybrid Working Arrangement.
(25)  For a Hybrid Working Arrangement to be approved, the following must be able to be demonstrated:
  1. the staff member will be able to satisfactorily complete the requirements of their role split across the periods in which they are working remotely and in attendance at campus;
  2. where there are certain functions, activities or duties that can only be performed on campus, the staff member attends on campus to perform those functions, activities or duties; 
  3. where there are specific events or activities that the University requires the staff member to attend for on campus, they will be required to be on campus for those times. Events or activities will not be created for the purpose of making it difficult for staff to work remotely;
  4. workplace health and safety requirements are able to be met; and
  5. the needs of the local work unit are able to be met and the arrangement does not unreasonably impact upon other staff.

(29)  The staff member must submit a written request for a Hybrid Working Arrangement, (that is outside of to the Ways of Working model) to their supervisor by email at least four (4) weeks before the arrangement is proposed to commence. The staff member’s email must:
  1. detail the reason for their request; and
  2. demonstrate that it complies with clause 24 above, with consideration for the following: 
    1. productivity gains or losses;
    2. ability to attend on campus where required by their role;
    3. the potential impact on their team and other relevant staff;
    4. that workplace health and safety requirements will be met; and
    5. impact on operational requirements and the needs to the local work unit.

(43)  There may be occasions when a staff member's personal circumstances change or there is a strategic need, and the staff member may need to apply to for an Interstate or Overseas Work Arrangement to temporarily relocate to work remotely interstate or overseas.
(44)  Requests will be considered on a case-by-case basis. Requests for Interstate or Overseas Work Arrangements need to be submitted in writing by the staff member to their supervisor:
