  1. Immediate consultation with the Injury and Workplace Support Consultant;
  2. Where practicable, ensuring that rehabilitation and return to work activities commence immediately, or as soon as possible to ensure the earliest possible return to pre-injury employment;
  3. Ensuring that effective procedures are in place to support early, safe and durable return to work;
  4. Where practicable or legislatively required, ensuring return to work duties, including modified or alternate duties, are made available where practicable to assist the injured staff member to remain at work;
  5. Maintaining the confidentiality of information relating to staff participating in occupational rehabilitation in accordance with privacy legislation;
  6. Ensuring that return to work information is maintained accurately and correctly in accordance to relevant privacy and WorkSafe guidelines.

