(9)  Appointees will be leading practitioners in their professional fields who must be able to contribute in a translational capacity to the teaching and research efforts of the University by translating research, or the pedagogy of research, into practice in the broad public sector.
(10)  Criteria for appointment:
  1. Level E appointees normally would be leading proponents with an international reputation; 
  2. Level D appointees would be leading proponents at least at national level; 
  3. Must have recognised and demonstrable level of competence as judged by their peers and be leading practice in elite settings;
  4. Appointees would not necessarily have a PhD but normally would have a Masters qualification;
  5. Evidence of research productivity, which may differ from that expected for a standard academic appointment, but esteem factors would be high;
  6. Must be practising at the time of appointment and continue to practice and maintain registration while at the University;
  7. If retired, they should be moved to another category, such as adjunct appointments.

(12)  Appointments will be:
  1. Remunerated at the respective salary rates for Level D or Level E academics;
  2. Fractional, normally 0.4 to 0.6 FTE;
  3. Fixed term for two years and renewable.

