  1. A rationale for making such an appointment and what the expectations for the role will be; 
  2. Job card and position description;
  3. Funding source, internal or external;
  4. a copy of the proposed appointee’s curriculum vitae;
  5. the names and contact details of three disciplinary experts who could attest to the proposed appointee’s national/international standing and their effectiveness in translating research into practice;
  6. Proposed selection committee membership (refer to section below).


(15)  If the proposal is supported by the Vice-Chancellor or the Chief People Officer (respectively), a selection committee will be appointed. 
(16)  The selection process will be similar to that for a standard Level E or Level D appointment (refer to standard selection procedures for relevant level). Normally this would entail interviewing the candidate.

