(16)  All other students must use the Application for Remission of Debt or Fee Liability Form (available from the [Student Forms webpage](https://www.latrobe.edu.au/students/admin/forms/search)) and include:
  1. a clear and detailed Statement of Personal Circumstances (see Part A);
  2. documentary evidence from a professional or authority, that independently verifies the details of a change in personal circumstance, and clearly: 
    1. identifies the change in personal circumstance;
    2. dates the occurrence of the change in personal circumstance;
    3. dates the duration of fullest impact of the change in personal circumstance; and
    4. provides a professional or clinical assessment of the level of impact of the change in personal circumstance on the student’s capacity to complete the subject or withdraw by the Census Date.
  3. additional supporting documentary evidence should be relevant to one or more of the following categories (as per section 14 of the Administration Guidelines): 
    1. medical;
    2. family or personal;
    3. employment-related;
    4. course-related.


(17)  Provision of a statutory declaration or a medical certificate is not sufficient. At a minimum, a detailed letter from a medical professional must include:
  1. date of the consultation, and whether a diagnosis is based on an examination by the practitioner or a self-report by the student;
  2. either a new clinical diagnosis, or a circumstance that exacerbated a pre-existing condition, and when this first became evident or was predictable;
  3. the severity of impact on the student’s ability to continue studies, or to withdraw by 11.59pm AEDT on the approved Census Date for the relevant teaching period; and
  4. the dates and duration of the fullest impact of the circumstance.


(18)  Documents in languages other than English must be translated by a NAATI-accredited translator, with both the original and a certified copy provided.

(22)  If the University knows, or believes, that a student has provided false or misleading information in their application for remission of debt or fee liability, the University:
  1. will notify the student immediately and cease assessment of the application;
  2. may take reasonable steps to verify the authenticity of the documentation provided by a third party, including by contacting that third party directly (e.g. a medical practitioner);
  3. may refer the matter for consideration under the [General Misconduct Statute 2009](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/directory/summary.php?legislation=37) and the [Student Conduct Management Policy](https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=382); and
  4. may notify the Department of Home Affairs where appropriate.

(23)  The Manager, Academic Services (as the Nominated Officer) will notify the applicant of the outcome by email as soon as practicable.
(24)  A notification will include:
  1. the name of the Nominated Officer;
  2. the reason for the decision;
  3. the steps to be taken to apply for a fee refund, where applicable; and
  4. advice concerning when and how the applicant may seek a formal internal review of the decision.

(28)  A student may seek an internal review of a decision made under this Procedure. The University’s Reviewer may reconsider the decision where satisfied that there is sufficient reason to do so. A formal request for review must:
  1. be written in response to the initial outcome notification;
  2. be received by the University within 28 days after the date of notification of the decision;
  3. set out the reasons for making the request, for example, why and how the applicant considers the initial application was not assessed in line with due process, this Procedure and/or legislation; and
  4. provide any relevant additional evidence that was not available at the time of application.


(29)  The Reviewer is an officer who was not involved in the original decision and who is senior to the officer who made the original decision. The Reviewer, is nominated by the Director, Academic Services and is currently the Deputy Director, Academic Services.

