(11)  For the purpose of this Policy:
  1. orientation programs: informational, academic and social activities that normally occur in the week prior to commencement of classes each semester, designed to facilitate students’ transition to La Trobe via engagement with their courses, their peers and their learning communities;
  2. student transition: an ongoing process of integration and engagement with university life, both academic and social, that occurs for students on the commencement of study, throughout their studies and as they complete and graduate from study;
